[gd_scene format=3]

; ── hd2d_lighting_concept.tscn ────────────────────────────────────────────────
; STANDALONE PROTOTYPE — not referenced by main.tscn, cabin_main.tscn, or any
; door transition. Open this scene directly (F6 / "Run Current Scene") to
; preview the HD-2D lighting mood without touching gameplay scenes.
;
; What this demonstrates:
;   • Octopath-style diorama camera: narrow-ish FOV, angled down, fixed.
;   • Y-axis billboarded quads standing in for Player / Plant / Station —
;     they always face the camera around the vertical axis only, and they
;     ARE shaded (not unshaded), so they catch real directional light and
;     cast/receive shadows like true HD-2D sprites.
;   • DirectionalLight3D + Environment ambient/fog tint driven live by
;     HD2DLightingRig from the actual real-time planetary hour — same data
;     source as ClockHUD and the main-menu orrery. The rig finds its
;     siblings via @onready $Path, so no manual wiring is needed here.
;   • Glow (bloom), near+far Depth of Field (tilt-shift diorama blur), and
;     ACES filmic tonemapping — all supported in the project's current
;     GL Compatibility renderer. (SSAO/SSR/SDFGI are NOT used here — those
;     require Forward+ and are deliberately avoided.)
;
; Debug controls while this scene is running:
;   [P]  cycle through all 7 planets instantly (bypasses the real clock)
;   [L]  return to Live — resume following the real-time planetary hour
;
; Migration notes for later (not done here):
;   • Existing Basil_idle_*/walk_* sheets are already 4-directional and can
;     feed a Sprite3D/AnimatedSprite3D per facing, or a shader that swaps
;     frames by camera-relative facing — no new art needed to prototype.
;   • Player/PlantNode/StationNode would move from CharacterBody2D/Area2D to
;     CharacterBody3D/Area3D. RoomManager's tile-coordinate logic (Vector2)
;     is engine-agnostic and needs no changes.
;   • TileMapLayers (Ground/Walls/Counter-tops/Rooftops) would be replaced by
;     3D floor/wall meshes; door Area2D→Area3D, same target_scene/spawn_point
;     metadata convention.

